<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <!-- LatestMajor, not LatestMinor: type providers erase to the analyzed
         project's RUNTIME references, and a net8 host handed lib/net10.0
         SQLProvider assemblies cannot instantiate them ("SqlDataProvider is
         not defined" on a project that builds cleanly). Running on the
         newest installed runtime lets the tool typecheck projects that
         target it; machines with only net8 still run on net8. -->
    <RollForward>LatestMajor</RollForward>
    <!-- ships as a dotnet tool: dotnet tool install fsharp-refactor -->
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
    <ToolCommandName>fsharp-refactor</ToolCommandName>
    <PackageId>fsharp-refactor</PackageId>
    <Description>Applies the FSharp.Refactor analyzers' quick fixes to F# code from the command line. Point it at a project, a script, a solution, a directory or a glob; --dry-run reports without editing. The tool clarifies the (agent-generated or old) code's intent, reduces non-alphanumeric noise, and uses built-in .NET libraries more efficiently.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>0.8.44: FR0101 gives nested index loops over different collections different element names (both took `item`, the inner one shadowing the outer). FR0164 reads the target runtime: `Dictionary.Remove`/`Clear` pass from .NET Core 3.0, an indexer overwrite and `HashSet.Remove`/`Clear` from .NET 5; on .NET Framework and netstandard all of them are reported. FR0092 leaves a message a test embeds in a longer string.

 0.8.43: Visual Studio extension bundles FsAutoComplete 0.85.3, whose quick fixes are titled by what they write. VS Code extension offers to install or update the `fsautocomplete` tool when Ionide&apos;s is older than 0.85.

 0.8.42: FR0075 counts a window the scope does not show modally (`form.Show()`, `Application.Run form`, a method of its own that shows it) as self-active: a `use` there disposed the window on the spot (C# twin CR0060).

 0.8.41: New rules FR0175 (date format `hh`/`mm`/`MM` mix-ups, fix), FR0176 (date parts from two instants, fix), FR0177 (always-true/false comparison pair), FR0178 (`.Value` in the empty branch), FR0179 (discarded immutable update), FR0180 (`Random` per call to `Random.Shared`, fix), FR0181 (specific catch around a blocking wait). FR0067 covers `Convert.To*` on a string, FR0017 `let _ = asyncCall`, FR0127 credential-named literals; reports mask credential findings. FR0049 accepts a read behind a bounded `Task.WaitAny`. Faster sweeps: files are no longer typechecked twice, and the project-wide use list is built once. `--api-changes` reads a referencing project only when its sources name the declaration.

 0.8.40: FR0055 stays quiet on a catch-all with a `when` guard, on the exception or on state (`with _ when stopping -&gt; ()`); only `when true` is still noted.

 0.8.39: `--define` (and `&quot;defines&quot;` in fsharprefactor.json) defines preprocessor symbols for the whole run: every MSBuild, script and `--parse-only` compilation. A script&apos;s `#r` of the project counts only where its `#if` nesting is live; one under an undefined `#if` names the symbol to pass, and one naming a missing build is read against the project&apos;s sources.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>Tuomas Hietanen</Authors>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Thorium/fsharp-refactor</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Thorium/fsharp-refactor</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>fsharp;dotnet-tool;analyzers;refactoring;codefix;static-analysis;code-quality;linter;code-cleanup;sarif;mcp;mcp-server;ai;llm;agents</PackageTags>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Unlicense</PackageLicenseExpression>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="FileWalk.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Workspace.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Program.fs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Update="FSharp.Core" Version="10.1.201" />
    <!-- FSharp.Analyzers.SDK drags in 6.0.0, which is OLDER than the 8.0.0.0 a
         SQLProvider type provider asks for: its MySqlConnector fails to
         initialise against ours and the whole project reports as broken.
         Pinned forward so the provider's own reference resolves. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="8.0.0" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\FSharp.Refactor.Analyzers\FSharp.Refactor.Analyzers.fsproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
